{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## NOT CLOSEABLE — 1387 fixed the PROBE path only; the harness still has the defect\n\nI was about to treat this as a closure candidate on the strength of 'the fix landed in 1387'.\nVerifying first: **1387 (`3922f20d09`) changed exactly ONE file** — `scripts/jira_dc_epic_link_clear_probe.py`\n(+60/-3) — and added **no tests**. Scored against the five criteria:\n\n* **AC1 (readiness requires every `_REQUIRED_FIELDS` name, not a `serverInfo` 200)** — met for the\n  probe script, **NOT for the harness**. `tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py:127-140`\n  `wait_for_jira_dc_ready` still polls `/rest/api/2/serverInfo` until it answers. That is the exact\n  gate this bug is about.\n* **AC2 (bounded budget, self-diagnosing message with the observed inventory)** — met in the probe\n  (`_FIELD_POLL_INTERVAL_S`); not in the harness.\n* **AC3 (`_assert_project_capabilities` distinguishes 'not registered yet' from 'not offered by this\n  image')** — `conftest.py` was not touched by 1387; unverified at best.\n* **AC4 (probe and harness share ONE readiness definition so they cannot drift)** — **explicitly\n  UNMET, and now measurably worse.** Fixing only the probe CREATED the divergence this criterion\n  exists to prevent: the probe polls the field inventory, the harness polls `serverInfo`. Two\n  definitions, drifted.\n* **AC5 (a test pins that a system-only field inventory reads as NOT ready)** — **UNMET.** 1387\n  changed no test file. This ticket's own Testing section calls this 'the load-bearing assertion …\n  without it this stays a latent flake that only appears when a run happens to be fast'.\n\nThe probe script's own comment states the measurement that condemns the harness path: `serverInfo`\nwent green after **8m32s** and **one second later** the inventory was 27 fields, **all system**, no\n`customfield_*`. The harness survives today only because it happens to do slower work afterwards —\nwhich is the definition of a latent flake, not a fix.\n\n**Remaining work:** move the harness onto the field-based wait and give both paths one shared\ndefinition, plus the negative test. **Blocked on sequencing, not on design:**\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py` is inside the active blast radius of the DC parent-hierarchy\nstream ([rebar:9f26-66c2-14af-4223] / [rebar:4b9e-bcad-456a-4233]), so starting it in parallel would\ncollide. Queued behind that stream."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785887545075140001,"uuid":"08eecdc6-1cfd-4217-91a2-5cff4ea52dfb"}